194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 93 0 R
/T (One of the main benefits of live-feed virtual production is that it restores environmental context for on-screen talent. Although an iPhone-based pipeline does not display the environment on a large LED wall, the  ability to instantly review takes with the fully composited digital environment gives immediate and important feedback. In traditional green screen  setups, actors often struggle with spatial awareness and eyelines, relying on markers like tennis balls or tape. With a live composite, they can clearly understand scale, distance, and interactions, resulting in more natural, confident, and immersive performances.)
/E (One of the main benefits of live-feed virtual production is that it restores environmental context for on-screen talent. Although an iPhone-based pipeline does not display the environment on a large LED wall, the  ability to instantly review takes with the fully composited digital environment gives immediate and important feedback. In traditional green screen  setups, actors often struggle with spatial awareness and eyelines, relying on markers like tennis balls or tape. With a live composite, they can clearly understand scale, distance, and interactions, resulting in more natural, confident, and immersive performances.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
