1208 0 obj
<<
/Title (SwitchLight 3.0 AI encounters these data-less, clipped areas, it lacks the necessary mathematical foundation to accurately determine surface normals or albedo. In an attempt to compensate, the AI must computationally "hallucinate" the missing data. This leads to several visual deficiencies: severe edge artifacts, temporal flickering between frames, or a smooth, waxy appearance on subjects, which is a result of over-smoothing noise. Furthermore, when trying to relight these clipped regions during post-production, they are incapable of accurately reflecting the new digital lighting. The result is a visually jarring effect where the subject appears unconvincingly pasted into the scene, with specular highlights appearing unnatural or misaligned.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1041 0 R
/Prev 1354 0 R
>>
endobj
